# Platform Testing boundary declaration

The presence of this file marks the tree as a **Platform Testing** tree: the reusable
platform **plus** the real project data used to validate it.

    platform_core_data/     ->     tracked, and must stay populated

Enforced by `scripts/verifyBranchBoundary.js` (`npm run verify:boundary`, and `prepack`).

## What this guard is actually for

The dangerous direction is the **normal** one. `tool-development` was created by deleting
`platform_core_data` from the shared history, so promoting it here replays that deletion
unless the one-time baseline merge already rejected it — silently wiping every run, module
and piece of execution evidence, on a command that looks completely routine.

This declaration makes that failure loud: if `platform_core_data` drops below its expected
size on a tree that declares itself Platform Testing, the check fails before the loss can be
committed.

## Why a file and not a branch name

Anything branched from here inherits the declaration, so `feature/*` work cut from
`platform-testing` is covered too. A branch-name check would miss exactly those branches, and
would disable itself on a detached HEAD or after a rename.

| Branch | Declaration | `platform_core_data` |
|---|---|---|
| `platform-testing` and anything cut from it | `.platformdata` | tracked, deliberately |
| `tool-development` and anything cut from it | `.toolonly` | zero tracked files |

**A tree must never carry both.** Both present means `tool-development` was merged in without
rejecting `.toolonly`, and the check fails on the contradiction.

## Promotion

```text
feature/*  ->  tool-development  ->  git merge into platform-testing  ->  real validation
```

Tool source flows down. Project evidence never flows back — a Tool fix made while on this
branch is promoted by cherry-picking the Tool-owned files, never by merging this branch
backward.

See [`docs/BRANCH_MODEL.md`](docs/BRANCH_MODEL.md).

**Do not delete this file to make a check pass.** Deleting it removes the invariant, not the
violation.
